Each value is one byte immediate inside Scheme::Scheme(); alpha (0 = opaque in VGUI1) is
left as it was. vgui.dll is shared by every GoldSrc mod in the Half-Life folder, so their
VGUI1 menus take the purple too. Steam's "Verify integrity of game files" puts the stock
file back; run build.bat again afterwards.

Rollback: the original is kept as TSM\backups\ts_ui_originals_2026-10-19\vgui.dll and
inside ts\original.zip; restore_originals.bat puts it back.

Xash3D (H9XASH) does not load this file. It runs FWGS's open VGUI1, freevgui, built from
source with the same six colours -- see H9XASH\vgui.dll.patch.
